From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:02:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] leds: show the pattern with the highest priority, restore the next one
Description:
 An LED shows one pattern at a time. So far the last started pattern
 won and the end of any LED feedback turned the LED off, also when
 another feedback was still running on it (e.g. a reminder for a missed
 message and the end of a short notification pattern).
 .
 Every feedback type now has the priority property the LED feedback had
 (unused so far). FbdDevLeds keeps the requested patterns per LED and
 shows the one with the highest priority, the newest one among equal
 priorities; when it ends, the next one is shown again, and the LED is
 turned off only when no pattern is left.
 .
 A constant light (frequency 0) is written as a constant pattern, so it
 replaces a running blink pattern; setting only the brightness left the
 pattern trigger running the old pattern.
Author: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-28
